WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.170
Meet distinctUI. Black, white and grey…

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.862
then one mark that's yours.

00:00:07.212 --> 00:00:12.848
It's a free, open-source design system, made as a skill your AI can use.

00:00:12.848 --> 00:00:15.582
It's the look behind Version One.

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:17.577
First, the AI setup.

00:00:17.577 --> 00:00:22.594
In Claude Code, add the marketplace, then install the plugin.

00:00:22.594 --> 00:00:24.142
That's two lines.

00:00:24.492 --> 00:00:28.510
Using Cursor, Codex, or another coding agent?

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:32.500
One command adds the skill: npx skills add.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:39.587
In the Claude app, download the skill folder from GitHub, and upload it as a skill in your settings.

00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:45.430
Then just ask. Say what you're building, and your signature colour.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:48.463
Build the sign-in page in distinctUI.

00:00:48.463 --> 00:00:50.170
Our colour is blue.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.998
Claude follows twelve rules.

00:00:52.998 --> 00:00:56.979
Light only, one typeface, black pill buttons.

00:00:56.979 --> 00:01:00.756
And errors are black and bold, never red.

00:01:01.106 --> 00:01:03.664
Colour lives only on the mark.

00:01:03.664 --> 00:01:09.783
Pick one of five palettes: Signal, Mzansi, Earth, Coast, or Jacaranda.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:17.504
The mark stays dashed while your project takes shape, and turns solid once it ships, with a small version label.

00:01:17.854 --> 00:01:19.581
And it moves, a little.

00:01:19.581 --> 00:01:23.412
Rings draw in once, and pop solid the day you ship.

00:01:23.412 --> 00:01:27.693
It all switches off for people who ask for less motion.

00:01:28.043 --> 00:01:29.443
Need a head start?

00:01:29.443 --> 00:01:36.901
There are eleven templates: a launch page, a dashboard, a profile, pricing, sign-in, and more.

00:01:37.251 --> 00:01:38.829
Building an iPhone app?

00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:40.749
There's a Swift package too.

00:01:40.749 --> 00:01:45.973
Add it in Xcode, and your SwiftUI screens get the same look, font and all.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:51.722
distinctUI. Free, at distinctui.com.
